2026-09-24 — disk-backed /tmp must also be a mountpoint.

RED: one declared Python regression, no compiler errors. The common full-suite
init kept /tmp on ext4 but left it a plain directory. Frozen resolve_test.c:54
unshares its mount namespace and changes /tmp to MS_PRIVATE. Frozen
fs/namespace.c:do_change_type rejects !path_mounted(path) with -EINVAL.
Both fresh unchanged-original RED flights reproduce errno 22 before any of
88 subtests runs; the parser correctly records INVALID_OUTPUT, not PASS.

Minimal C: selftest-tmp-mount.c, reference-built by sealed GCC 14.2.0-19
with -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror, then again with -DSELF_BIND=1.
On BOTH actual kernels: plain directory -> private_rc=-1, errno=22, FAIL;
self-bound directory -> private_rc=0, errno=0, PASS. Both modes preserve
sentinel bytes, device/inode, ext4 type and mode 1777. A neighboring ordinary
directory still returns EINVAL. The test uses an isolated mount namespace,
cleans up its own objects, and reuses the existing 64 MiB diagnostic disk.
Expected REDs are not counted as successful original programs.

Repair: full-suite init self-binds /tmp after chmod, failing closed if mount
fails. It neither copies data nor replaces ext4 with tmpfs. Selected K7 mode
and /dev/shm retain their tmpfs behavior. Runtime metadata records the setup.
No kernel, module, upstream source, binary, assertion, timeout or filesystem
feature is changed. A new 850 KiB initramfs supplies the actual repaired init.

Unchanged originals, serial GCC/EvoCC paired flights on identical old/new disks:
  openat2:resolve_test                     88/88 PASS on each kernel
  openat2:openat2_test                    116/116 PASS on each kernel
  filesystems/statmount:statmount_test_ns   2/2 PASS on each kernel
  mount_setattr:mount_setattr_test         34/34 PASS on each kernel
Each of eight GREEN/control flights has a fresh nonce and orderly shutdown;
all four programs, 240 nested cases per kernel, zero FAIL/SKIP. The original
45-second wrapper timeout remains. Kernel/test disk hashes match before and
after each run (QEMU snapshot=on), and the resolve_test binary is identical on
both disks. These are targeted environment repairs, not new compiler credit,
new complete 970-program totals, a new Image, or K13/K14 acceptance.

239 K1 Python tests PASS; targeted Ruff and git diff --check PASS.
tools/gate-changed.sh 83073f4 --offline -j 2 selects no Rust crate, correctly;
both actual init builds also pass GCC -Wall -Wextra -Werror.

